title    Small Nocturne in D
composer Claude
about    A short Romantic nocturne for solo piano: a singing right-hand melody over a left hand that carries both the bass line and the harmony.
tempo    72      # slow, lyrical, quarter = 72
beats    4       # 4/4
steps    2       # eighth-note grid, 8 steps per bar

# One piano split into three voices so each layer can be balanced.
# melody: the right hand's singing line, kept in F#4..D6 so it always sits above the inner chords and is loudest.
voice melody piano vol=1.0 pan=0.15
# bass: left-hand fifth finger, struck on the downbeat (and at mid-bar when harmony changes) and held. With no bass player, this voice
# alone defines the root or inversion, so it is low (A1..E2) and moves mostly by step in the inversions (C2, B1, Bb1, A1) to make a real bass line.
voice bass piano vol=0.75 pan=-0.2
# inner: left-hand chord stacks on the offbeats of the stride-like pulse (beats 2-4), in F#3..E4, under the melody and above the bass,
# soft so the melody stays on top. Each stack holds the 3rd and 7th where present, so the harmony reads even though the bass is just one note.
voice inner piano vol=0.5 pan=-0.05

# A: bars 1-8, the theme. I - vi - IV - V7, then a chromatic descending bass (D C B Bb A) under the repeat, ending on a half cadence.
pattern A
melody | A4--- F#5-- E5 | D5-- C#5 B4--- | . B4 D5 G5 B5-- A5 | G5-- E5 C#5- A4- |
bass   | D2------- | B1------- | G1------- | A1------- |
inner  | .- F#3+A3+D4- F#3+A3+D4- F#3+A3+D4- | .- F#3+B3+D4- F#3+B3+D4- F#3+B3+D4- | .- G3+B3+D4- G3+B3+D4- G3+B3+D4- | .- G3+C#4+E4- G3+C#4+E4- G3+C#4+E4- |
# bar 6 is D7/C (C natural in bass and melody), bar 7 G/B to Gm/Bb (borrowed minor iv for color), bar 8 D/A to A7.
melody | A4--- F#5-- E5 | D5-- C5 A4--- | B4- D5 G5 Bb4- D5 G5 | F#5-- A5 E5--- |
bass   | D2------- | C2------- | B1--- Bb1--- | A1------- |
inner  | .- F#3+A3+D4- F#3+A3+D4- F#3+A3+D4- | .- F#3+A3+D4- F#3+A3+D4- F#3+A3+D4- | .- G3+B3+D4- .- G3+Bb3+D4- | .- F#3+A3+D4- .- G3+C#4+E4- |

# B: bars 9-16, the melody climbs to C#6/D6 for the climax, then a ii-V cadence home. Harmony: Bm, F#m/A, G, E7/G# to A, D/F# to G, Em7 to A7, D, D.
# The bass rises A1 G#1 A1 then F#1 G1, a stepwise line that drives toward the cadence.
pattern B
melody | F#5--- B5-- A5 | C#6-- B5 A5- F#5- | G5-- F#5 G5 B5 D6 B5 | B5- G#5- A5--- |
bass   | B1------- | A1------- | G1------- | G#1--- A1--- |
inner  | .- F#3+B3+D4- F#3+B3+D4- F#3+B3+D4- | .- F#3+A3+C#4- F#3+A3+C#4- F#3+A3+C#4- | .- G3+B3+D4- G3+B3+D4- G3+B3+D4- | .- B3+D4+E4- .- A3+C#4+E4- |
# bar 16: the inner pulse stops and the full chord is held while the melody rises through D major to D6 as a quiet close.
melody | A5- F#5- G5- B5- | E5- G5- C#5- E5- | F#5-- E5 D5--- | . A4? D5? F#5? D6--- |
bass   | F#1--- G1--- | E2--- A1--- | D2------- | D2+A2------- |
inner  | .- F#3+A3+D4- .- G3+B3+D4- | .- G3+B3+D4- .- G3+C#4+E4- | .- F#3+A3+D4- F#3+A3+D4- F#3+A3+D4- | F#3+A3+D4------- |

play A B
